## Structure Rules

- Root: only config/tooling files.
- All code in `src/`, entry: `server.js`.
- One domain = one module; modules isolated, no cross-module imports.
- Shared code in `lib/` only.
- Module names: kebab-case. Module files: `<module>.routes.js`, `.controller.js`, `.service.js`, `.repository.js`, `.schema.js`.
- Layers: Routes (map), Controllers (HTTP), Services (business logic), Repositories (DB/ORM). WebSockets: only in `websockets/`, called via services.
- Any dir with >1 util/helper: must have `index.js` barrel exporting all via `module.exports`.
- Barrel imports required (`require('@lib/foo')`), never direct subfile (e.g., `.../success`).
- Required barrel files: all `src/lib/*` subdirs, `src/config/`, any multi-file utility dir.
- No barrel needed for module subdirs (routes, controllers, etc.).
- `lib/`: only stateless, reusable utils.
- `config/`: only config/constants.
- `middlewares/`: global middleware, barrel optional.

## Forbidden

- Business logic in routes/controllers.
- DB access outside repositories/services.
- Cross-module imports.
- Feature logic in `lib/`.
- Circular deps.
- WebSockets in controllers/routes.

## Enforcement

- Any deviation: invalid.
- Refactors must reduce coupling/duplication.
- Structure is mandatory, applies project-wide.